Always read docs before coding.
Never violate documented rules.

================================================================
CORE RULES
================================================================

Teacher cannot register students.
Only Registrar can register students.
Parent Portal and Student Portal are cloud only.
Finance must use Double Entry Accounting.
No hard delete — soft delete only (deleted_at).
Everything audited — every mutation logged.
Outside school network: Admin, Director, Registrar, Teacher, Finance, HR, Inventory, Library, Cafeteria, Auditor become View Only.
Super Admin exempt from network restrictions.
Build only the requested phase.
Do not generate future phases unless explicitly requested.

================================================================
COMPLETED PHASES
================================================================

Phase 1 (Foundation): Docker, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Redis, SQLAlchemy, Alembic ✓
Phase 2 (Auth): Login, register, JWT, refresh, logout, forgot/reset password, RBAC middleware ✓

Phase 3 (License): ✅ seeds + verification logic in schema/models
Phase 4 (Registration): ❌ Not started

================================================================
ARCHITECTURE
================================================================

Backend: FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + PostgreSQL + Redis
Frontend: Next.js 15 + TypeScript + Tailwind + Shadcn
Auth: JWT (access + refresh tokens), bcrypt passwords
RBAC: 13 roles with permission matrix
Audit: Every mutation logged with old/new values, user, IP, device

================================================================
DATABASE CONVENTION
================================================================

All models use UUID primary keys (String(36)).
All models have created_at, updated_at, deleted_at (soft delete).
Relationships use string FKs with ForeignKey("tablename.id").
Use `from app.database import Base` for declarative base.

